      ms: 9560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:p682t9'
    '|a||In Boston in the 1990s, condo owners who faced selling at a loss asked noticeably more, and sold more slowly. That''s loss aversion in a real market.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1gplttd'
    '|b||And the investors, who do this for a living, showed about half the effect. Experience shrinks it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5560
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:q3g115'
    '|a||Half is not none. And a market doesn''t always punish a bias. A seller can profit from it instead, like a gym contract sold to the self we plan to be.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:if9qnu'
    '|b||Then the line runs here: with practice and quick feedback, biases fade. Once in a life, they can stay.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6640
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:xlmir7'
    '|a||How sure are we? That biases shrink with practice and feedback: mostly agreed.':
      mp3: 
